# Defect d-lane-room-mixedown-1 (lane room-mixedown, 2026-11-26; panel 260's
# R2 to R4, provisional, author ratification pending): in a program none of
# whose groups says `layer`, a name of the layer's that a header's text puts
# in the program's own code is told at the group whose header puts it there.
# `now.h` makes `now_ns` a macro for `hero_time_monotonic_ns`; until the
# repair it was told at the program's first group, `"a.h"`, whose `answer`
# reaches nothing of the layer, its guess fix replacing that group's string.
extern "a.h"
    function answer() -> i64

extern "now.h"  #~ ffi_layer_undeclared
    function now_ns() -> i64

function main()
    print(answer())
    print(now_ns() > 0)
